CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ handler completes: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
remove_cpp_exceptions cleared the in-flight exception of a catch(...)
handler after the handler's first instruction, so a call there ran with
the exception still in flight and, f being noexcept, ended in
std::terminate's assumption (the path was cut).  The first instruction is
now a SKIP.
